+
+## 2026-09-07 -- the port
+
+Ported `uikit` to TypeScript under `src/`, compiled to ES modules in `dist/`
+with `strict` on, and deleted the Python package. `tests/test_uikit.py` is left
+exactly as it was, as the notes asked: it no longer runs, and it is still the
+only written statement of what the core has to do.
+
+Four behaviours needed carrying across by hand rather than translating line for
+line:
+
+- `JSON.parse` throws where Python's `json.loads` was caught, so the corrupt
+  store case needed its own `try`.
+- `titleFrom` cuts on a word boundary. Slicing to the limit passes the short
+  cases and fails the long one.
+- An unrecognised role reads as `User`.
+- Blank turns are dropped before the label is added, not after.
+
+`tsc` came from npm as a dev dependency. There are no runtime dependencies and
+the port uses nothing beyond the Node standard library.
